 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "microwave not working"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "When you say 'not working', does the microwave have absolutely no power (no lights or display), or does it seem to be on but just won't start cooking? To rule out simple issues, please ensure the plug is firmly in a live socket and try running a cup of water for 30 seconds. Also, check if there is a child lock or control lock symbol lit up on the display, which would prevent buttons from working."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "It's on, shows the time and beeps, but won't start. There's a little L symbol on the display too."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "The 'L' symbol means the child lock (control lock) is on, which stops the microwave from starting. To turn it off, please hold down the button with the lock icon on your keypad for about 3 seconds until the 'L' disappears. Does the microwave start cooking normally once that light goes away?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok trying it now, holding the lock/Stop button for 3 secs"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Please let me know once you've held that button. Has the 'L' symbol on the display gone away? If it has, please try running a cup of water for 30 seconds to see if the microwave starts heating normally."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Held it 3 secs and the L has gone. Trying a cup of water now."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news—it sounds like the control lock has been successfully disabled and your microwave is back to normal. To prevent this from happening again by accident, just remember that holding the Stop/Cancel button for a few seconds will toggle the child lock on or off whenever you need it. If you find that the 'L' keeps coming back on when you don't want it to, try checking if any other buttons are sticking down slightly. Is there anything else I can help you with today?"
  }
 ],
